From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:22:40 -0500
Subject: feat: a swipe shows the next Space beside the one on screen

While the fingers move, the two-finger Space swipe on the Mac now draws the
Space it would bring in beside the one on screen, its title and list joined
a list's width away on the side it comes in from, and moves the two
together, both at full strength. Swiped back past where it began, the Space
the other way is drawn instead. Lifted far enough, the Space comes in from
where it was drawn; lifted short, the drawing goes back out with the list.
Before, only the Space on screen went with the fingers, fading to 40%, and
the next one showed only once they lifted (spaces B35).

The drawing is made inside one task: SpaceModel::ScopedDrawnSpace has the
model answer for the next Space while the visibility controller lays out its
rows and title, the list is scrolled where that Space was left (B48), both
are recorded as the switch's outgoing Space is, and the Space on screen is
put back before anything is painted. Nothing is activated, selected, woken,
saved or told. With the keyboard's focus on a sidebar row nothing is drawn,
since hiding the row for the drawing would move the focus.

Why: the owner, 2026-11-24, on 0.7.1: the next Space did not show while
swiping, as it does in Arc.
Removable when: never; this is Stedding's own behaviour.
